{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["And the meaning of <b>ויאמר משה</b> [Moses said] is as I shall show it to you, and I shall ask it. And its meaning: Moses had already told them this thing — do it: they shall bring a goat and a calf and a lamb and an ox and a ram, then the glory of HaShem will appear to you. And the meaning concerns the fire that went forth."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {0 "The phrase 'כאשר הראיתיך ואשאל אותה' (as I shall show it to you, and I shall ask it) is elliptical; rendered hyper-literally as the syntax stands, without smoothing."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:09:15.069153054Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}